## Key Corrections

- New Grid2D simulation stages can compile and show a valid DataInterface binding while not writing to the Grid2D. A constant-circle positive path must prove the exact stage writes before trusting wave math.
- The template `AdvectGrid` preserved input is the old curl-advection sample, not the current-cell sample. The wave solver must explicitly call `SamplePreviousGridVector4Value(Unit, P)` for the current cell.
- Normal RT validation must use per-channel background-mode deviation. A flat packed normal can read back as `[188, 188, 255]`, so a fixed `[128, 128, 255]` baseline marks the whole RT active.
- Client `sleep` did not advance the editor simulation at the expected frame rate in this harness. The successful validation uses `advance_simulation` without any post-advance `set_paused` call.

## Remaining Work

- Visual tuning in PIE is still a user gate: strength, normal strength, damping, and water window size may need adjustment.
- Demo/controller behavior should be checked from PIE after this solver replacement because this report validates the Niagara system and production RT, not every Blueprint gameplay path.
